course: dictionary
lesson: 8742
title: Serve, a word with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one you need. Serve can mean to give food, to help or work for someone, to start play in a game, or to deserve something. «At the table you wait until everyone is seated and served» is about food, because people sit at a table and wait for their meal to be given to them.
explain: The clues in a sentence show you the right meaning. «While Toad was in prison, the river-bankers stood up for him, but the Wild Wood animals said it served him right» means they thought he deserved his bad luck. Ask yourself: what word fits here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Serve also appears in maths. A dish that «serves 4» is enough food for 4 people. To work out how many dishes you need, divide the people by the number served, then round up, because you cannot cook a part of a dish for the extra people.
fact: Serve is a verb, and serves, served and serving are its other forms.
fact: A serve is also a noun: in tennis, the serve is the hit that starts the point.
fact: «Served» can mean given food or drink, as in «everyone is seated and served».
fact: «It serves you right» means you deserved the bad thing that happened to you.
fact: First come, first served means people are dealt with in the order they arrive.
exercise: «At the table you wait until everyone is seated and served.» What does served mean here? | Carried away to the kitchen | *Given food or drink | Counted by the cook | Cleaned up after the meal
exercise: A pizza serves 4. How many pizzas do 10 people need? | *3 | 2 | 10 | 4
exercise: «It serves him right» means what? | He won the game | He was asked to cook | He was given a present | *He deserved it
test: In tennis, what is a serve? | Running to the net | *Hitting the ball to start play | Catching the ball after it bounces twice | Counting the points
test: Which phrase means people are helped in the order they arrive? | Serve and volley | Served on a plate | *First come, first served | Serve it up, hot and fresh
exam: «Marco Polo said he served Kublai Khan for 17 years.» What does served mean here? | Wrote letters about | *Worked for and helped | Ate meals with | Fought against
